id: file_delete
category: file_io
difficulty: 3
libs:
checker: exact
timeout: 10
--- prompt
Write an Objeck program that creates a file named llm_eval_delete.txt in the current directory containing the text `temp`, prints whether the file exists (true or false), deletes the file, and prints whether it exists again. Output is two lines: `true` then `false`. Use System.IO.Filesystem's File class for the checks.
--- expected
true
false
--- reference
use System.IO.Filesystem;

class FileDelete {
	function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
		name := "llm_eval_delete.txt";
		FileWriter->WriteFile(name, "temp");
		File->Exists(name)->PrintLine();
		File->Delete(name);
		File->Exists(name)->PrintLine();
	}
}
